{
  "id": "T6_stops_effort",
  "title": "Loop stops per variant and block",
  "population": "TRAJECTORIES",
  "unit": "trajectory",
  "notes": [
    "TRAJECTORIES: the repair trajectory of one base cell under one variant: iterations 0..final_iteration, terminal status from the loop's own state ledger.",
    "Stop statuses are trajectory facts, NOT success metrics; R09 counts trajectories that requested a repair, not successful repairs (R02 in T5/T5b).",
    "R07 equals the R06 stopped_budget share and R08 the R06 stopped_analysis_incomplete share (identical counts, checked); both are shown under their own metric ids.",
    "R09 repaired_share: meaning = trajectories that requested at least one repair (final_iteration >= 1); numerator = trajectories; denominator = trajectories; unit = trajectory.",
    "IC6: static_feedback repair triggers are dominated by clang-tidy bugprone findings and, on MPI, by low-confidence hints (design document: no trustworthy static MPI tool exists); static_feedback results measure this frozen blocking-set configuration, not static analysis in general."
  ],
  "definitions": [
    {
      "ref": "R06 stop_status_distribution",
      "text": "R06 stop_status_distribution: numerator = trajectories; denominator = trajectories; unit = trajectory."
    },
    {
      "ref": "R07 budget_exhaustion_rate",
      "text": "R07 budget_exhaustion_rate: numerator = stopped_budget; denominator = trajectories; unit = trajectory."
    },
    {
      "ref": "R08 analysis_incomplete_stop_rate",
      "text": "R08 analysis_incomplete_stop_rate: numerator = stopped_analysis_incomplete; denominator = trajectories; unit = trajectory."
    },
    {
      "ref": "R10 iterations_used",
      "text": "R10 iterations_used: numerator = sum of final_iteration; denominator = trajectories; unit = trajectory."
    }
  ],
  "ci_note": null,
